# Text is kept with LF in the repository, whatever the computer that commits it: a Windows
# checkout without core.autocrlf would commit CRLF, which `cargo fmt --check` passes (as
# WordCraft found). What Git takes for binary is left as it is.
* text=auto

# Test files whose exact bytes matter (signed and encrypted MIME parts end lines in CR LF): no
# line-ending conversion on checkout.
crates/pgp/testdata/** -text
